--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/configuration.rst
@@ -0,0 +1,42 @@
+Configuration
+=============
+
+All configuration options are set in your Sphinx ``conf.py``.
+
+``typehints_strip_none_return``
+-------------------------------
+
+**Default:** ``False``
+
+When set to ``True``, if a function's return type annotation is ``None`` or
+``NoneType``, the ``:rtype:`` block is **completely omitted** from the
+generated documentation — no ``:rtype:`` field is emitted at all.
+
+This is different from ``typehints_document_rtype_none`` (see below):
+
+- ``typehints_strip_none_return = True`` — the entire ``:rtype:`` block is
+  removed; the field does not appear in the output.
+- ``typehints_document_rtype_none = False`` — the ``:rtype:`` block is still
+  generated, but the type content is hidden (rendered as an empty field).
+
+Example:
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+   # conf.py
+   typehints_strip_none_return = True
+
+With this setting, a function annotated as ``def foo() -> None:`` will not
+have any ``:rtype:`` entry in its documentation.
+
+Interaction with other return-type options
+~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+
+- ``typehints_strip_none_return`` takes priority over
+  ``typehints_document_rtype_none``.  When both are set and the return type is
+  ``None``, the ``:rtype:`` block is completely omitted.
+- ``typehints_document_rtype = False`` disables *all* return-type
+  documentation regardless of this option.
+- ``typehints_use_rtype`` controls whether the return type appears as a
+  separate ``:rtype:`` block or is inlined with ``:return:``.  It has no
+  effect when ``typehints_strip_none_return = True`` because no return-type
+  information is emitted at all for ``None`` returns.
